{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113292","id":3054710576,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc62Ey8w","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113292","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113292.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113292.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113292","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113292/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113292/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113292/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/46c3a1d857bc0a4fe55500ffd3ba91f7b6f2768b","number":113292,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Use additive blending for suns in ProceduralSkyMaterial to fix dark suns","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This prevents dark DirectionalLight3D colors from creating splotches in the sky, which is a commonly encountered issue when working on day/night cycle systems.\r\n\r\nThis affects how bright suns are rendered too, with a greater impact on heavily saturated colors.\r\n\r\nIf we consider the visual difference to be too important, we'll probably want to add a **Sun Blend Mode** property to control this (although ProceduralSkyMaterial is already quite complex as it is). If we want a compatible solution that still addresses the original issue, we could perform premultiplied alpha blending instead, with the \"alpha\" value being determined by the color's HSV value.\r\n\r\n- See https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/13748.\r\n\r\n**Testing project:** [test_sky_sun.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23828339/test_sky_sun.zip)\r\n\r\n## Preview\r\n\r\n*The scene has 4 suns.*\r\n\r\nBefore | After\r\n-|-\r\n<img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Screenshot_20251128_193658\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8c7caf2c-732f-4671-9262-f353312bb28e\" /> | <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Screenshot_20251128_193706\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0b3a3454-628e-42ba-933c-11b6e01c8f32\" />\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":955079684,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw5NTUwNzk2ODQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/breaks%20compat","name":"breaks compat","description":"","color":"b64245","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.gi